  "question": {
    "text": "A marble block of mass $2 \\mathrm{~kg}$ lying on ice when given a velocity of $6 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ is stopped by friction in $10 \\mathrm{~s}$. Then the coefficient of friction is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xhXm7",
      "text": "\n$0.02$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2zF4A",
      "text": "\n$0.03$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cVedb",
      "text": "\n$0.04$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XRIJ6",
      "text": "\nNone of  these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$a=\\mu g=\\frac{6}{10}$             [ using $\\mathrm{v}=\\mathrm{u}+\\mathrm{at}$ ]\n$\\Rightarrow \\mu=\\frac{6}{10 \\times g}=\\frac{6}{10 \\times 10}=0.06$",
    "image": null
  },
